<title>ARMENIA: SOCCER-PUNIC YEREVAN RETAIN ARMENIAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PUNIC YEREVAN RETAIN ARMENIAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>YEREVAN 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Punic Yerevan retained the</p>
<p>Armenian league title with a win at the weekend which put them</p>
<p>out of reach of their closest rivals ahead of the final day of</p>
<p>the season on Tuesday, officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>Title winners and runners-up since the Armenian championship</p>
<p>was formed in 1992 after the collapse of the Soviet Union (to</p>
<p>1994 spring-autumn, 1995-96 onward autumn-spring):</p>
<p>		Champions		Runners-up</p>
<p> 1992	 Shirak Gyumri	  Punic Yerevan</p>
<p> 1993	 Ararat Yerevan	 Shirak Gyumri</p>
<p> 1994	 Shirak Gyumri	  Omentmen Yerevan</p>
<p> 1995-96    Punic Yerevan	  Shirak Gyumri</p>
<p> 1996-97    Punic Yerevan	  To be decided</p>
<p>Ararat Yerevan won the Soviet championship in 1973, the only</p>
<p>Armenian club ever to do so in the 55-year history of the Soviet</p>
<p>league from 1936 to 1991.</p>
</text>
